 "briefing": "# Nvidia Meeting Briefing: 17 November 2026\n\n**Research window:** 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Status of This Briefing\n\nNo verified changes at Nvidia for 16 October to 15 November 2026 could be confirmed. Every search attempt returned \"No valid search results found\" or a parameter error, so no news, product launches, executive changes, or deals were retrieved, and none are reported here. This is a tool failure, not evidence that nothing happened. The sections below are placeholders to be completed through the manual checks listed at the end.\n\n## News\n\nNo press coverage or company announcements from the window have been verified. Nvidia's newsroom and investor relations site should be checked for releases dated 16 October to 15 November 2026. Items should be added only after each has a direct URL and date.\n\n## Product and Technical Launches\n\nNo product launches, major technical updates, or software releases from the window have been verified. Nvidia's official blog (blogs.nvidia.com) and developer blog (developer.nvidia.com/blog) should be checked for posts in this period.\n\n## Executive and Notable Hires or Departures\n\nNo executive appointments, departures, board changes, or senior hires from the window have been verified. The most authoritative check is Nvidia's SEC filings on EDGAR. Form 8-K filings with Item 5.02 disclose officer and director changes, and Form 4 filings disclose insider transactions. Nvidia's CIK is 0001045810.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo partnerships, acquisitions, investments, customer agreements, or supply agreements from the window have been verified. Nvidia's newsroom, investor relations site, and 8-K filings are the primary places to confirm any deal, with business press as secondary confirmation.\n\n## Manual Verification Checklist (Before 17 November)\n\n1. **Newsroom:** Review press releases dated 16 October to 15 November 2026 at nvidianews.nvidia.com.\n2. **Blog:** Review product and technical posts at blogs.nvidia.com and developer.nvidia.com/blog.\n3. **Investor relations:** Review earnings materials, event calendar, and filings at investor.nvidia.com.\n4. **SEC EDGAR:** Filter Nvidia's Form 8-K, Form 4, and Schedule 13D/13G filings for the window at sec.gov.\n5. **Business press:** Search for Nvidia coverage in the window, and confirm each item against a primary source before use.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting (Provisional)\n\nThese questions are not yet grounded in verified changes. They should be revised once the checklist above is complete.\n\n1. Have any product launch dates or roadmap priorities changed since mid-October 2026, and how might they affect our planned work together?\n2. Have there been any changes to the executive team, business unit leadership, or board that would alter our points of contact or decision authority?\n3. Which recent customer, supply, or partnership agreements are relevant to our engagement, and what timelines do they set?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Nvidia Newsroom (verification source, not verified for window content): https://nvidianews.nvidia.com\n[2] Nvidia Blog (verification source, not verified for window content): https://blogs.nvidia.com\n[3] NVIDIA Developer Blog (verification source, not verified for window content): https://developer.nvidia.com/blog\n[4] NVIDIA Investor Relations (verification source, not verified for window content): https://investor.nvidia.com\n[5] SEC EDGAR (verification source, not verified for window content): https://www.sec.gov",
